<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oyake Akahachi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oyake Akahachi was a chieftain on Ishigaki Island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaeyama-islands">Yaeyama Islands</a> who led resistance to the Ryukyu Kingdom at the end of the fifteenth century. He refused tribute and rejected Shuri's interference in local religion, and in 1500 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-shin">Shō Shin</a> sent a large fleet that defeated and killed him. The victory brought the Yaeyama Islands firmly under Shuri, and Akahachi is honoured locally as a hero.</p></div>
